# Project Requirements — Android WebView App Template

## 1. Purpose

Create a reusable Android application template for converting existing
websites and public GitHub web projects into customized Android apps.

The project must support a workflow based on an Android phone, GitHub,
and GitHub Actions, without requiring Android Studio on the phone.

## 2. Supported Application Types

### Mode A: Remote Website
Load an existing HTTPS website inside an Android WebView.

### Mode B: Bundled Website
Package HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and other frontend assets inside the APK.

Use AndroidX WebKit WebViewAssetLoader for safe local-content loading
where appropriate.

### Mode C: Hybrid Application
Bundle the frontend while connecting to an online backend, API,
authentication service, or database.

Document all internet and backend requirements.

## 3. Customization

The template must support configuration of:

- Application name
- Android application ID
- App icon
- Splash screen
- Start URL
- Website loading mode
- Allowed website hosts
- Theme colours
- JavaScript and storage settings
- External link handling

Customization must be documented and reliable.

## 4. WebView Features

Implement and test:

- Website loading progress
- Android back-button navigation
- Network error handling
- Appropriate website navigation restrictions
- Cookie and storage support when required
- File uploads and downloads where supported
- External browser and application links
- Appropriate handling of login redirects
- Optional offline functionality when supported by the website

## 5. Security

- Use HTTPS by default.
- Do not bypass TLS certificate errors.
- Do not enable cleartext HTTP by default.
- Avoid unrestricted JavaScript-to-native bridges.
- Avoid unsafe local-file access settings.
- Restrict navigation to trusted hosts where practical.
- Never commit API keys, passwords, or signing credentials.
- Review third-party licences before copying or redistributing code.

## 6. Android Build System

The repository must include:

- Complete Android project source
- settings.gradle.kts
- build.gradle.kts
- App-level Gradle configuration
- gradle.properties
- gradlew
- gradlew.bat
- gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties
- gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
- AndroidManifest.xml
- Required resources and source files

All required Gradle wrapper files must be committed to GitHub.

Do not assume that uploading files from a phone preserves
the gradle directory or JAR files.

## 7. GitHub Actions

Provide automated workflows to:

- Validate the project structure
- Run available tests
- Build the Android debug APK
- Report build failures
- Upload the APK as a downloadable artifact

The basic workflow should not require paid services or private API keys.

## 8. Documentation

Create:

